# What fans do. Start the AppHost first (dotnet run --project dev/AppHost) and publish an event
# with BackOfficeApi.http. Run the requests top to bottom: each one uses values from the ones before.

@publicApi = http://localhost:5101
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180

### Browse: published events that haven't started, soonest first (no sign-in needed)
# @name list
GET {{publicApi}}/events

### Search event and venue names (web search syntax: "quoted phrase", -excluded)
GET {{publicApi}}/events?q=demo arena&pageSize=10

### The first event's page: venue, prices, sales phase, seat-map URL
# @name page
GET {{publicApi}}/events/{{list.response.body.$.items[0].eventId}}

### Its seat map, at the versioned URL from the event page (cached for good)
GET {{publicApi}}{{page.response.body.$.seatMapUrl}}

### What's free: places per section, and the free seats (Inventory; the client joins them with the seat map on seatId)
# @name availability
GET {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/availability

### Sign in as ana, a fan (password grant, development client only)
# @name ana
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=ana&password=ana

### Hold two free seats (all or none). For the best free places instead: { "section": "A", "quantity": 2 }
# @name hold
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "seatIds": [ "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[0]}}", "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[1]}}" ] }

### Changed your mind? Release the hold (then hold again; one hold per fan per event)
# DELETE {{publicApi}}/holds/{{hold.response.body.$.holdId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Check out: returns the order and the LocalPay page to pay on (open redirectUrl in a browser)
# @name order
POST {{publicApi}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holdId": "{{hold.response.body.$.holdId}}" }

### After paying: the order's status (Pending until LocalPay's webhook confirms it)
GET {{publicApi}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}
